    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asks for a `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>` (YY = last two digits of the `registrationDate` year). Since this value is derived purely from the owner's own already-stored fields (`customerCode` + `registrationDate`) \u2014 the test comment even notes it's \"seed-independent\" \u2014 I implemented it the same way the existing derived fields `displayName` and `initials` are done, rather than adding a DB column or pipeline step:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   `registrationDate` is always non-null by the time the owner is mapped (`BuildOwner` defaults it to the current date). The `%02d` matches the test's `substring(2, 4)` extraction (e.g. year 2026 \u2192 `26`, year 2005 \u2192 `05`).\n\nBoth the new `AcceptanceTest.coreMembershipNumberFormat` and the full build pass.",
